    {
      "id": "setup-starter-cut-and-his-heels",
      "title": "The starter card and 'His Heels'",
      "kind": "rule_paraphrase",
      "edition_ids": ["two-player-standard-en"],
      "topics": ["setup", "starter", "his-heels"],
      "summary": "After the crib is laid away, the non-dealer cuts the remaining deck and the dealer turns up the top card of the lower packet as the starter. If the starter is a Jack, the dealer immediately pegs 2 points, called 'His Heels' (or 'His Nibs' in some references). The starter is not played to the tabletop during the play phase but does count as a fifth card in every hand and in the crib when they are scored.",
      "source": {
