      "topics": ["board", "peg", "score-tracking"],
      "summary": "The board has four rows of 30 holes split into two per-player tracks, plus game holes at one end where the pegs start. Each player uses two pegs of one color. To record a score the rearmost peg leapfrogs the frontmost peg forward by the number of points scored, keeping the previous position visible for correction. Custom is to go 'down' (away from the game holes) on the outer row and 'up' the inner row; the standard 121-point game is 'twice around' the board.",
